  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The table below provides the peak emission wavelengths <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda_{\\text{max}}\"></span> for two stars, Rigel and Betelgeuse, which can be modeled as blackbody radiators.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Star</th><th>Peak wavelength <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda_{\\text{max}}\"></span> / nm</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Rigel</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"240\"></span></td></tr><tr><td>Betelgeuse</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"840\"></span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>The surface temperature of Betelgeuse is approximately <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"3500 \\text{ K}\"></span>. What is the surface temperature of Rigel?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1000 \\text{ K}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"12250 \\text{ K}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"3500 \\text{ K}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"42875 \\text{ K}\"></span></p></li></ol>"
